      "question": "Simplify: $\\dfrac{a^3 \\cdot b^2 \\cdot c^4}{a^2 \\cdot b^3 \\cdot c}$ and express in simplest form.",
      "answer": "$\\dfrac{a c^3}{b}$",
      "options": [],
      "glassboxSteps": [
        {
          "rule": "Quotient law",
          "why": "$\\frac{x^m}{x^n} = x^{m-n}$.",
          "math": "\\dfrac{x^m}{x^n} = x^{m-n}"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Apply to each base",
          "why": "Subtract exponents for $a$, $b$, $c$.",
          "math": "a^{1} \\cdot b^{-1} \\cdot c^{3}"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Simplest form",
          "why": "Write negative exponent as reciprocal.",
          "math": "\\dfrac{a c^3}{b}"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Quotient law: $\\frac{ac^3}{b}$.",
      "linked_note_id": "CH02-sec-exponents-and-powers",
